#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cube_root

#% text
# `cube_root(x)` gives the real cube root of the real number `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For negative `x` the result is negative, unlike `x^(1/3)` which gives the principal complex root.

#% item
# Complex `x` gives the principal root.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cube_root(-27)
#% output
#= -3

#% cell
cube_root(128.)
#% output
#= 5.039684199579492

#% cell
cube_root(18)
#% output
#= 2^(1/3)*3^(2/3)

#% cell
n(cube_root(18), 40)
#% output
#= 2.620741394208896607141661280441996270239428

#% cell
cube_root(-4.5)
#% output
#= -1.6509636244473134

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `surd`, `sqrt`
